title: Proposition 34
---
order: 34
---
short_label: I.34
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In parallelogrammic areas the opposite sides and angles equal one another, and the diameter bisects the areas.
----
proof:

Let {ACDB|CABD} be a parallelogrammic area, and {BC} its diameter.

I say that the opposite sides and angles of the parallelogram {ACDB|CABD} equal one another, and the diameter {BC} bisects it.

